      "message": "As someone that only had cursory glances at what the bug was about, I still feel pretty out of the loop even after reading this CL. Maybe a bigger CL description here would help.\n\nFrom what I can tell: you have an overvoltage problem, so instead of letting the ln9310 do its own startup we override a few of its \"procedures\" by using those 4 registers (though we used those 4 registers for something else before, so now we have to live with a small loss of functionality?).\n\nAll of that should be in this commit message, but in better words than mine.",
